# FFA Phase 7: Real-Conditions Pass — Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** Make FFA hold up outside headless tests:
- fix the known in-maze frame-time doubling;
- visually verify the parts only checked in code (remote players, spectator, end screen, rematch);
- measure bandwidth;
- give the owner a one-click local 4-window launcher;
- finish the docs.

**Architecture:**
- **Maze visibility:** `FfaWorld.ApplyVisibility(Vector3 viewerWorldPos)`. When the viewer is inside a maze body (not its hallway), every OTHER maze's builder node is hidden (`Visible = false`: rendering and lights only; collision stays). Otherwise all mazes are shown. The online arena calls it on its 0.2 s zone tick, using the local player's position, or the spectated puppet's while spectating. `FfaLocalArena` calls it too, so the offline perf harness can measure it.
- **Bandwidth:** additive `BytesSent`/`BytesReceived` counters in NetworkManager.
- **Windowed verification:** one windowed client (the host) plus three headless clients runs `TestFfaMatchFlow`/`TestFfaRematchFlow` with `--shot <dir>` to save screenshots at key moments.

